{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-326c-7266-b5ef-3a9e6baa2d6d","id":"01a1a64d-7757-71d9-a09c-94bcfd6d1fbf","idempotency_key":"03c15575b803da2af547b53ff09d1a6306eee334abf13e477bd6da1256b83c91","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:24:17Z","payload":{"note":"Docs plus two clients that drive a real server, not a stub. docs/mcp.md covers the Claude Desktop and opencode stdio configurations, the HTTP endpoint with its token and the literal curl call, the tool surface, the approval return shape and the poll, the resource uris, and the limits that matter (no chat/settings/provider keys, one shared queue and audit log with the app). apps/rusty-brick-chess/tests/mcp/mcp_stdio_client.js spawns 'rusty-brick-chess mcp', initializes, sees 31 tools, runs a read, then asserts a write returns approval_required with an id it polls back as pending. mcp_http_client.js puts the refusals FIRST - no token 401, wrong token 401, rbc://board/../../etc/passwd refused - before the happy path, then the read, the approval_required write, and rotation leaving the old token 401 and the new one 200. scripts/check_mcp.sh builds, seeds a scratch database, runs both and prints MCP_SUITE_PASS; check_all.sh calls it, so the 'one suite command' item is true rather than aspirational. The first run failed and the CLIENT was wrong, not the server: create_board takes workspace_id and fen, not parent_kind/parent_id/start_fen - worth remembering that a mock client is code with its own bugs and a red result is not automatically a product defect.","target":"t-3241"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
